/// Lore fragments (the Builders' story), with their era.
pub static LORE: [(Era, &str); 12] = [
    (Era::Golden, "We raised our halls from the bones of the hills, and the hills did not mind. Every stone was laid by hand, and every hand was proud."),
    (Era::Golden, "The roads of the Builders ran from the ice to the sand. A traveller could walk a whole season and never leave a street."),
    (Era::Golden, "Our elders said there was no shape the world could not be given. We believed them. We were right, for a time."),
    (Era::Golden, "Those who would not build left for the river valleys and lived simply. We pitied them. Now I envy them."),
    (Era::Expansion, "Beneath the desert we found a door that was not a door - a frame of stone that showed fire on its far side. We named the place beyond it the Burning Realm."),
    (Era::Expansion, "From the Burning Realm we carried emberstone. It does not dull, it does not break, and it is warm to the touch, always."),
    (Era::Expansion, "The sea took the tower at Low Harbour in a single night. We said it was the tide. The tide had never done that before."),
    (Era::Expansion, "With emberstone our tools could cut anything. And so the council asked: what lies past the fire? What is the farthest place?"),
    (Era::Deep, "Those who returned from the Silent Realm do not speak. They stand in the dark and move stones from place to place, as if building something only they can see."),
    (Era::Deep, "We call them the Hollow now, though they were our sisters and brothers. They do not like to be looked at. I think they remember."),
    (Era::Deep, "Something waits in the Silent Realm. We woke it by reaching for it. It is not angry. It is patient. That is worse."),
    (Era::Deep, "If you are reading this, you are not one of us, and you are not one of them. Follow the old roads. Find the gateways. End what we began."),
];
